IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ba-traveller`

-- Biosecurity Act 2015 (Cth), with the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014 ss 82, 84, 103 -- worked cases
-- from the seat of the incoming traveller.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case, the goods determinations under ss 173, 174 and 182, the Biosecurity Regulation 2016, the approved form of
-- the incoming passenger declaration, or the Quarantine Act 1908 that applied in 2011.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_biosecurity-act-2015_baseline.py). Expected
-- results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts the lives do not state are ASSUMPTIONS, labelled where used: that Chloe is in the prescribed class and was required
-- to fill in the declaration (it is handed out on the flight); that she arrived on 1 July 2011 (the life gives only the
-- year); that her souvenirs are caught by no determination. Whether a good is prohibited, suspended or conditional is an
-- INPUT (the determinations are not deposited). The beef jerky and the other variants are ILLUSTRATIVE, not from the lives.
-- A penalty unit is taken as 330 dollars (the s 4AA figure before indexation): ILLUSTRATIVE.

